  "takeaways": {
    "uz": "Applied to Uzbekistan without any Uzbek data, the naive splice jumps ×4.88 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.77, a locally refitted one ×1.15 (MODIS alone ×1.35). In 2012–2019 the KZ model is off by 35.5% a month and -32.4% in total; the same model refitted on Uzbekistan: 17.7% and -0.4%. Uzbekistan's VIIRS/MODIS ratio is ×3.94, the KZ model implies ×2.66: VIIRS sees relatively more fires there (C1: small agricultural burns). 2025 contains the new industrial source near 38.1°N 67.3°E (C2), so the holdout is also shown to 2024 — it changes little.",
    "tm": "The naive splice jumps ×4.75 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.66, a locally refitted one ×1.02 (MODIS alone ×1.21). Overlap error as-is 42.3% (bias -34.9%), local refit 22.9%. 57% of Turkmenistan's confident detections are static sources (Kazakhstan 13%); FIRMS `type` removes them in archive data and the mask in recent data (precision/recall above). The remaining error is the same kind as Uzbekistan's: VIIRS/MODIS ×4.16 vs ×2.70 from the KZ model. TM's monthly R is the lowest of the cell-level countries.",
    "annual": "Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan have only a few hundred fire cell-days a year, so only annual totals are meaningful. KGZ: annual error 9.2%, bias -5.7% (raw MODIS: -72%); TJK: annual error 20.3%, bias +19.6% (raw MODIS: -76%). The harmonized totals are usable for a yearly trend, not for single months.",
    "transfer": "Transfers as-is: KAZ, KGZ; does not: AUS, BRA, IND, PRT, TJK, TKM, USA, UZB. The observed VIIRS/MODIS ratio ranges from ×1.58 to ×4.46; the KZ model cannot know a country's ratio and errs in the direction of the difference (too high for Portugal, too low for India). Refitted locally, the same model gets 5.2–37.4% monthly error. Honest conclusion: the METHOD transfers across biomes, the COEFFICIENTS do not — every country needs its own 2012–2019 overlap fit (which FIRMS provides everywhere).",
    "ba": "Holding burned area fixed, naive: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in none; KZ-harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ; locally harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ, TJK, TKM, UZB. The naive series jumps ×2.2–×5.8 everywhere. Correlation with burned area is high in Kazakhstan and weak in Kyrgyzstan/Tajikistan (few fires; much burned area there is not seen as active fire).",
    "events": "Kostanay forest and steppe fires (Auliekol) (2022-09): 91 cell-days in one hexagon vs a normal of 1, rank 412 of 1255. Abai region forest fire (Semey Ormany) (2023-06): 123 cell-days in one hexagon vs a normal of 0, rank 242 of 1255. The top events are the largest local excesses; check them against news before the demo."
  }
